# Review routing for the catalog.
#
# This repository distributes executable content. SECURITY.md tells reviewers to "treat any
# PR touching `implementations/` as a code-execution change" and to read the whole script
# rather than the diff hunk -- and until this file existed there was nothing routing such a
# PR to a reviewer at all. Human review is named as the only control between a malicious
# pack and a git hook on someone else's machine, so the routing for it has to be mechanical.
#
# CODEOWNERS alone requests reviews; it does not require them. That takes "Require review
# from Code Owners" in branch protection on `main`.
#
# GitHub applies only the LAST matching pattern, so order is significant and the specific
# entries below must stay after the default. They name the same owner today, which makes
# them documentation of what is sensitive rather than a different routing decision. That is
# the point: when a second maintainer joins, `*` moves to the wider group and these lines
# keep executable content and the trust documentation where they are, without anyone having
# to work out which paths mattered.

# Everything, unless a more specific rule below overrides it.
* @open-coder-ai

# Executable content. Installed by `chock add`, these become a git hook that runs on
# every commit in an adopter's repository and a guard consulted before their coding agent
# runs a command. Two policies ship one today (block-destructive-commands, block-no-verify);
# the pattern covers any policy that grows one later.
/base/*/implementations/ @open-coder-ai

# The gate scripts CI depends on. `gen_policy_docs.py` and `check_readme.py` are what stop a
# policy page claiming a control the policy does not have, so a change here can disable the
# check that catches an overclaim without touching the overclaiming file.
/tools/ @open-coder-ai

# CI, issue and PR templates. A workflow change can remove every check above it.
/.github/ @open-coder-ai

# The trust model an adopter reads before deciding to install anything from here.
/SECURITY.md @open-coder-ai
